# Kan: rules for anyone (person or AI) working on this repo

1. Read `docs/PROJECT_GUIDE.md` first: it is the map of the engine (data model, turn loop, prompts, clock, canon, images, invariants in §13).
2. Work on `master` in `xanpire/kan` and push after each finished change; no pull requests. Bump the version in `package.json` and `app.json` together and run `node scripts/generate-sw.js`.
3. Before every push: `bun run typecheck` and `bun run test` (strict invariants on). Every bug fix gets a regression test in `scripts/`.
4. Keep the architecture: two-call turns (narrator prose, then the state tracker), pure apply functions, the job queue. Fix the function named; don't rewrite.
5. No new libraries without a reason: no stock photos, no state or data-fetching libraries. UI text about Kan is second person, and the UI never shows what Kan couldn't know.
